# V.32bis at 9600 trellis with MNP class 4 over it, 8 Sep 2026 -- the
# first V.32 call that carried an interactive session rather than a
# banner and then noise.
#
# What this one pins is the fix that made it possible.  A level in
# Modec.QAM.RevTracker is a correlation over the tracked mean square of
# the input, and that average is slow, so a signal returning after a gap
# reads high for two or three blocks while it catches up.  One such
# block used to convince the calling modem that the far end had gone
# back to the start of Figure 4, so it went back to AA -- which this
# board answered by restarting for real, and the two of them went round
# the start-up together until the call timed out.  Every "no rate signal
# R3" and "no E from the answering modem" against 2600.network was that.
#
# The recording contains the board restarting once for real, so a
# regression in either direction shows up here: too eager and the
# livelock comes back, too slow and the genuine restart is missed.
source:    recordings/20260907T233626-+15642442600.wav
seconds:   30.0
role:      originate
modes:     v32bis,v32,v22bis
v8:        yes
mnp:       4
connect:   V32bis 9600
expect:    https://2600.network - Patton 3120 #1
expect:    uSerNaME:
tolerance: 0
